<section id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center">
      <h2 class="h2">A few questions <em>you might have</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="faq-col">
        <details><summary>Do I need to register to listen to the podcast?</summary><div class="a">Nope! All four episodes are free on Apple Podcasts, Spotify, or wherever you listen. Signing up is only for the live finale on Thursday.</div></details>
        <details><summary>Do I need to be techy to get something out of this?</summary><div class="a">Not at all! This series is made for practitioners who aren't technical. We keep it simple and skip the jargon.</div></details>
        <details><summary>Is this for local or virtual practices?</summary><div class="a">Both! In Episode 3, we get into how your strategy changes depending on which one you are, and on the live call we're auditing one of each.</div></details>
        <details><summary>Is the live call free?</summary><div class="a">Yep, it's totally free.</div></details>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-col">
        <details><summary>Do I have to submit my site to sign up?</summary><div class="a">Nope! The audit is optional. You can register for the call and send in your questions without submitting a site.</div></details>
        <details><summary>How do you pick the 2 sites to audit?</summary><div class="a">When you sign up, say yes to the audit question and tell us a bit about your practice. We'll choose 2 practices from those requests and let you know before the call if you're picked.</div></details>
        <details><summary>What if I can't make it live?</summary><div class="a">Sign up anyway and submit your question ahead of time. The taping airs on the podcast Monday, Nov 2.</div></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
